# =============================================================================
# Root .gitignore — repo-wide belt-and-braces.
# backend/, frontend/, grader-frontend/ each have their own .gitignore with
# project-specific rules; the patterns here apply everywhere as a safety net.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets: never commit, no exceptions -----------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# Google Cloud service-account keys
gen-lang-client-*.json
service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
!package-lock.json

# --- Claude Code: machine-local settings (permissions) ----------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Node -------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- OS / editor junk -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Internal planning material (owner ruling 2026-09-09) -------------------
# Plans, specs, PR briefs, mission reports, trackers and design mockups stay
# OUT of the repo. Both remotes are PUBLIC, and this material is working
# context — not something the codebase needs in order to be built or run.
#
# ANCHORED to the repo root (leading `/`): documentation that belongs to the
# project lives under `docs/`, and nothing here may reach into it.
/PLAN_*.md
/PLANS_*.md
/PR_*.md
/PR5_*.md
/REPORT_*.md
/MISSION_*.md
/TRACKER_*.md
/CENSUS_*.md
/CAPACITY_PLAN_*.md
/GraderAgent_sprint_plan.md
/DESIGN_RECOVERY_SUITE.md
/batch_redesign_LOG.md
/vivi-*-spec*.md
/vivi-*-plan.md
/vivi-*mockup*.html
# One-off measurement dumps from a single investigation.
/schema_attest_pre_wipe.txt
/c1_payload_measurement.txt
